---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/12-09/', brochure='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/c33b7289-cdf6-4ce9-8754-c86248544bbb/EN_product-info_Elyra-7.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS Elyra 7 · passive image comparison" description="Inspect a stationary Elyra 7 and compare contrast in two synthetic images of the same inert grating." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ely"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-09/">← Equipment 12-09</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ely-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">12-09 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & STAGED IMAGES / FIRST PASS</span><h2>ZEISS Elyra 7</h2><p>Orbit the inactive microscope. Switch between two staged images of the same artificial grating and measure what changed: contrast improves in the narrower blur, while pitch and orientation stay the same.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Inactive inverted microscope</h3><div id="ely-view" aria-label="Orbitable documentary ZEISS Elyra 7 with Axio Observer 7 SR, exterior module and two camera housings"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-ely-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-ely-view="optics">Stand and detector</button><button data-ely-view="display">Teaching display</button><button id="ely-cycle">Next image track</button></div>
<p id="ely-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal pad on the generic display desk changes the teaching image only.</p></section>
<section><h3>Fixed synthetic image comparison</h3><canvas id="ely-plot" width="700" height="400" aria-label="Staged grating shown on a common relative intensity scale"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Image track<select id="ely-track"><option value="wide">Wide blur</option><option value="narrow">Narrow blur</option><option value="flat">Constant control</option><option value="missing">Missing comparison</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="ely-inspect">Inspect frequency and contrast</button><button id="ely-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="ely-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a staged comparison and inspect its pixels.</p><output id="ely-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="ely-png" disabled>Display PNG</button><button id="ely-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="ely-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: ZEISS Elyra 7 on an inverted Axio Observer 7 SR stand with Duolink and two ORCA-Fusion BT detector housings, documented by <a href={brochure+'#page=21'}>ZEISS product information Rev. 3.1, p. 21</a> and the <a href="https://scopem.ethz.ch/center/instruments-alphabetical/Zeiss_Elyra7.html">ETH Zurich system configuration</a>. The <a href={brochure+'#page=22'}>ZEISS exploded system overview, p. 22</a> establishes exterior component relationships and the nominal 1,200 × 900 mm system table plan. Table height, housings and generic display desk are visually inferred, not measured. The optional incubator and internal paths are omitted.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original whole setup render with table, white microscope and generic display"/><figcaption>Original whole instrument render, not a photo. Rev. 3.1, p. 22 anchors the system-table plan and assembly layout.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original close-up of eyepieces, stage, inactive module and paired camera housings"/><figcaption>Original close-up compared with the Rev. 3.1, p. 21 product image. The silhouette, stage, and twin exterior camera housings are approximate.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Table plan</td><td>1,200 × 900 mm</td><td>Metric model anchor. Height 860 mm assumed, not a documented tolerance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fixed image grid</td><td>64 × 64 square, 0.10 µm sample spacing</td><td>A synthetic coordinate system, not camera settings.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Grating vector</td><td>0.911086 cycles/µm; 30.963757° CCW from +X</td><td>Both staged grating images agree within 10⁻⁹. Stripes are perpendicular to this vector.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contrast</td><td>0.160199938 wide; 0.594208032 narrow</td><td>Measured by the selected Fourier peak relative to the mean; both agree within 10⁻⁹.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Constant and missing</td><td>Neither yields a frequency</td><td>Distinguished as a real flat array versus an absent input.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Patterned-frame reconstruction with dropped phase handling</td><td>Not run or implemented. The missing track is an absent fixed image, not a missing SIM phase.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The passive synthetic data use a single sinusoid with integer bin vector (5,3) on a 6.4 µm square. The ideal Gaussian low-pass transfer magnitude is <code>exp(−2π²σ²|f|²)</code>; the authored contrast 0.7 is attenuated by σ = 0.30 and 0.10 µm. A separable discrete Fourier analysis estimates each selected track from its pixels. It uses a common contrast scale and a canonical half-plane to resolve the ±frequency symmetry. This is not SIM or SIM² reconstruction, calibration, or actual illumination. No biological input, imaging procedures, hardware settings or measured resolution are included.</p>
<p><a href={base+'elyra7-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'comparison-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-09/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ely{max-width:76rem}.ely .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.ely section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.ely .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.ely .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.ely label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.ely input,.ely select,.ely button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.ely button{cursor:pointer}.ely button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.ely .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.ely #ely-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.ely #ely-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ely #ely-plot,.ely img{width:100%;height:auto}.ely #ely-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.ely #ely-status.error{color:#a54a34}.ely .scroll{overflow:auto}.ely table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.ely td,.ely th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.ely figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.ely .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
